claimed: okay-script-forms -- operator ask 2026-09-07: typed forms from Schema for pages, both roads. (1) Live.form[A](submit: A => String, checks*)(using Schema[A]): a Live app whose view is okay-ui's Form.ofWith[A] plus a Submit button, whose update is Form.edit / Form.errors / Form.decode, and which calls `submit` with the DECODED A -- mounted like any Live app. (2) the plain HTML road, no JavaScript: api.Forms.html[A](action, value, errors) renders the same Schema-derived tree as a <form method=post> with name= attributes, and api.Forms.read[A](Web.current.form, checks*) folds the posted fields through Form.edit (dotted keys, sums, lists -- the wire's own edit site) and decodes; errors are per-field data to re-render with. A checkout example in examples/site. Touches api/Live.scala (+Forms.scala), specs/okay-script.md; no build.sbt change.
